WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.110
Today i play the role of an expert in urban
planning, no, jokes aside, let's talk about

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:10.810
the mega-project to build the new administrative
capital of Egypt, announced by President Al-Sisi

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:16.129
at the international economic conference held
in Sharm el Sheik in March 2015.

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:20.800
There are many opinions about it: there are
those who consider it necessary to attract

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:26.619
foreign investors and realize a sort of Dubai
2.0 and those who instead consider it a waste

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:27.619
of money.

00:00:27.619 --> 00:00:29.010
But let's go step by step.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.809
The first attempts to transfer the government
center to the middle of the desert date back

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:36.440
to the second half of the 1970s.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:41.379
Due to the demographic boom and the rapid
growth of the urban agglomeration, President

00:00:41.379 --> 00:00:47.850
al-Sadat decided to build a new administrative
capital named after him in 1978, precisely

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.250
59 miles north-west of Cairo.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:55.239
Actually, before him, a similar thing had
been done by president Nasser when, with the

00:00:55.239 --> 00:01:00.660
enlargement of Heliopolis district, he founded
Nasr, which today is a soburb but according

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.250
to the initial projects it should have represented
the new Egyptian capital.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:11.130
However Sadat's city maneged to grow for a
short period and also hosted some ministries,

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:16.520
including that of Housing, which remained
there for 8 months before returning to Cairo

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.350
after the assassination of al-Sadat himself.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:24.510
The development of the city was totally abandoned
during the era of President Mubarak, as its

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:29.560
population barely reached one hundred fifty
thousand and most of the buildings that were

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:35.340
originally assigned to the ministries were
converted to house the newly established Menoufia

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.340
University.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:41.530
Finally in 2014, the government of President
Al-Sisi dusted off plans for a new capital,

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:47.439
making it one of the priority objectives of
the development strategy named "Egypt 2030"

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:51.430
and which today raises several doubts about
its sustainability.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:56.539
The strong interest in the project is witnessed
by the progress it has made in recent years

00:01:56.539 --> 00:02:01.939
and many experts agree that two are the fundamental
reasons behind the revival of this ambitious

00:02:01.939 --> 00:02:06.460
idea: the first is the need to legitimize
the presidential government in the eyes of

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:11.370
the population and the second is the intention
to move government institutions away from

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.530
the center of Cairo.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:17.390
Theater of episodes such as the Arab Spring
unrest and the coup that led to the fall of

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:20.519
President Mohamed Morsi in 2013.

00:02:20.519 --> 00:02:25.810
Let's talk about the project: after the failure
of the negotiations with Kuwait, Saudi Arabia

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:31.440
and United Arab Emirates and after the lack
of Chinese support for some differences on

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:36.560
the financial framework adopted, the Egyptian
government decided to make the first move

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:41.860
on its own by drawing on the national budget,
through a team of architects and designers

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:45.900
united under the name of Urban Development
Consortium +5.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:51.160
In reality, Chinese companies have never completely
disappeared, but their investments (for a

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:56.510
declared amount of 1.2 billion dollars) are
nothing more than limited loans: these funds,

00:02:56.510 --> 00:03:02.099
in fact, can only be spent on Chinese-sourced
equipment, including material for a new metro

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:06.769
system that should connect the new capital
to Cairo and for what will be the tallest

00:03:06.769 --> 00:03:11.739
tower in Africa, partially assigned to the
China State Construction Engineering Corporation.

00:03:11.739 --> 00:03:17.459
While the company in charge of construction
and management of the entire city is Administrative

00:03:17.459 --> 00:03:21.830
Capital for Urban Development (ACUD), whose
majority share is in the hands of the Ministry

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:26.860
of Housing (51%) and the remaining 49% in
the hands of the Armed Forces.

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:32.580
Rising from the sands 27 miles east of Cairo
towards the Suez Canal, the New Capital is

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.280
the last and largest desert city promoted
by the rejiim.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:41.920
But enterprises of this magnitude aren t unusual
in Egypt, and past regimes have always considered

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.299
them the panacea for all ills.

00:03:44.299 --> 00:03:49.120
As for example the Great Aswan Dam was seen
as the final solution to the problem of the

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:53.750
distribution of the waters of the Nile, so
in our case the new capital claims to solve

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:57.950
the problems of unemployment, transportation
and overpopulation.

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:02.440
The promises are many: to lighten the load
on the real estate market of Greater Cairo,

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:07.770
to accommodate the city's growing population,
to reduce pollution and traffic congestion.

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:12.120
So the government has presented the New Capital
as a pole of attraction for international

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:15.000
investment and a center of economic growth.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.120
Thanks to the industrial drawings, we can
get an idea of the layout of the future city:

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:24.240
an area covering over two hundred seventy
square miles (275), 68 of which have been

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:30.730
developed in the first phase until 2018, intended
to accommodate over 6 million Egyptians (6.5).

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:35.810
It is divided into several sectors: that of
the Wedian residential neighborhoods, divided

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:41.520
into high, medium and low density zones (which
will rifl ct the future costs of the housing

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:46.570
units there) with educational services and
social and health infrastructure; the business

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:52.020
district, consisting of offices, an industrial
area and a solar farm (a solar park that is

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:57.740
expected to cover 70% of the city's energy
needs); a complex of parks with a serpentine

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:03.211
shape that intends to imitate the course of
the Nile River for an extension of 9.6 square

00:05:03.211 --> 00:05:09.140
miles; a large airport; then we have the government
district, which will host ministries and public

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.590
offices and finally the presidential palace.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:16.010
For the way it is structured it looks like
an urbanized part of the agglomeration of

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:21.040
Cairo (the so-called greater network, which
includes several satellite cities) and this

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:25.900
is derived from the fact that the megaproject
will not have its own governorate, but will

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:30.290
fall instead under the administrative responsibility
of the governorate of Cairo.

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:35.490
All this for the modest sum of between 45
and 58 billion dollars.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:38.740
But is everyone in agreement on achieving
such a feat?

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:43.700
Obviously not, there are different lines of
thought but let's talk about how the government

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:48.110
justifies such an expenditure of human and
economic resources.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:52.660
Supporters see in such an ambitious project
the birth of a Dubai of the Mediterranean,

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:56.810
perfect for attracting national and foreign
investments and tourism.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:06:01.480
Taking Dubai as a point of reference is not
wrong, especially if we consider the image

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:06.480
that the Emirates metropolis has managed to
offer in the last 40 years, with the tallest

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:11.700
skyscraper in the world, enormous artificial
islands and the largest airport in the Middle

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:12.700
East.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:14.110
And what are the unofficial reasons?

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:19.080
Al-Sisi wants to use the new capital to strengthen
his position, winning over the private business

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:24.380
sector and gaining back the popular support
that had sustained him during the bloody crackdown

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:26.480
on the Muslem Brotherhood movement.

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:31.320
In fact, recent events such as the devaluation
of the national currency (the pound), the

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:36.460
repression of critical voices, the increase
in fuel prices and the border clashes with

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:41.710
Sudan, have left their scars on the legitimacy
of the president and his administration.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:47.230
Instead, the 2011 revolution that led to Mubarak's
downfall is important in understanding why

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:52.310
the move of government institutions is so
imminent; it was originally scheduled for

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:55.130
2019 but postponed due to the pandemic.

00:06:55.130 --> 00:07:00.850
The revolution was primarily urban and gained
momentum due to the popular mass concentrated

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:05.900
in Cairo where networks and media allowed
civilians to organize and mobilize quickly.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:12.020
This resulted in a huge wave of people emerging
from the center, nearby areas, historic parts

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:17.270
and even the wealthiest neighborhoods to gather
in symbolic places such as Tahrir Square,

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:23.210
the cradle of the Arab League's HQ, the center
of Egyptian bureaucracy Mogamma, the Nasser-era

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:28.220
Nile Hilton Hotel and finally the headquarters
building of Mubarak's National Democratic

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:29.220
Party.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:34.070
Same procedure was followed during the coup
that deposed President Morsi in 2013.

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:39.130
Therefore, the current regime is well aware
of the iconic power of the Square and this

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:44.540
explains the aspiration of the authorities
to abandon the old and overpopulated Cairo

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:48.870
and move to their happy oasis in the middle
of the desert, far from the people they have

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:51.360
to govern and from their unpredictable movements.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:56.690
If the displacement of the institutions is
now confirmed, can we say the same about entire

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:58.740
families of ordinary citizens?

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:02.190
Who will be able to live in the new capital
once completed?

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:04.670
The prices of housing units are prohibitive.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:09.670
Think that a two-bedroom apartment costs about
fifty thousand dollars, a huge sum that is

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:15.040
out of reach for many in a country where the
GDP per capita is about three thousand dollars.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:19.670
The big risk then, unless the government takes
appropriate action, is that the new capital

00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:24.840
will act as a cage for the rich and do little
to meet the needs of poor and disadvantaged

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:25.840
residents.

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:30.720
This is why the New Administrative Capital
is already seen by many as a colossal waste

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:32.180
of resources.

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:36.570
Critics say that it would have been better
to spend that money on improving living conditions

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:42.010
in the poor parts of the old capital or even
better to reduce regional disparities across

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:47.700
Egypt by providing services, job opportunities
and projects to improve the overall quality

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:48.700
of life.

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:53.180
In response to these criticisms, the authorities
have stated that the city will also include

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:58.090
social housing, but didn t provide details
on when it will be built and made available

00:08:58.090 --> 00:08:59.180
to those in need.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:03.710
All of this brings to mind the regime of Hosni
Mubarak and his downfall.

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:08.780
The last decade of his government was supported
by the rise of wealthy capitalist lobbies

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:13.450
that helped the economy grow, but prevented
the benefits of this growth from reaching

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:15.330
the poorest sectors of society.

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:21.060
And indeed, one of the most prominent slogans
in the January 2011 protests that overthrew

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.460
the Mubarak regime was "social justice."

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:28.080
Who knows if history will repeat itself, one
thing is certain, Al-Sisi's new fortress will

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:31.850
make the hypothetical uprising just a little
more difficult to accomplish.

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:36.330
Well, we are done for today, I hope i gave
you a clear idea of what will happen soon

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:41.000
in this part of North Africa, we will hear
about it again in the near future.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:42.170
See you in the next video.

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:42.260
Bye

